{"name":"Mild Heart Attack","hex":"#f27362","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mild","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Gentle and not easily angered.","Of only moderate severity; not strict."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A relatively low-gravity beer, often with a dark colour; mild ale"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mild"},{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"},{"term":"attack","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An attempt to cause damage, injury to, or death of an opponent or enemy.\n\n Any of several specific maneuvers, skills, or special abilities that a character can use to inflict damage against opponents.","Any of several specific maneuvers, skills, or special abilities that a character can use to inflict damage against opponents."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply violent force to someone or something.","To aggressively challenge a person, idea, etc., with words (particularly in newspaper headlines, because it typesets into less space than \"criticize\" or similar)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/attack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Myocardial infarction","blocks":[{"text":"A myocardial infarction (MI), commonly known as a heart attack, occurs when blood flow decreases or stops in one of the arteries of the heart, causing infarction to the heart muscle. The most common symptom is retrosternal chest pain or discomfort that classically radiates to the left shoulder, arm, or jaw. The pain may occasionally feel like heartburn. This is the dangerous type of acute coronary syndrome."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Blausen_0463_HeartAttack.png/330px-Blausen_0463_HeartAttack.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myocardial_infarction","wikidata":"Q12152"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Heart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg/500px-Heart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Heart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg/1280px-Heart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Heart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg/500px-Heart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross section showing anterior left ventricle wall infarction","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHeart_ant_wall_infarction.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Patterns_of_topo